#### Variation 1: SMART on FHIR for Azure APIM + Okta + HAPI FHIR (Primary Pattern)

**Description**: Enterprise-grade SMART implementation using Azure API Management as gateway, Okta as identity/OAuth provider with SMART extensions, and HAPI FHIR as FHIR server. This is Gainwell's standard implementation for new state deployments.

**Architecture**:
- **API Gateway**: Azure API Management Premium with OAuth JWT validation policies
- **OAuth Server**: Okta Authorization Server configured with SMART-specific scopes and launch token support
- **FHIR Server**: HAPI FHIR 6.x on Azure Kubernetes Service (AKS) with SMART interceptors
- **Identity**: Okta for members, Azure AD B2C for providers
- **Token Storage**: Azure Cache for Redis (distributed token cache and revocation list)

**Implementation**:

```xml
<!-- Azure APIM Policy: SMART Token Validation and Patient Compartment Enforcement -->
<policies>
    <inbound>
        <!-- Extract JWT from Authorization header -->
        <validate-jwt header-name="Authorization" failed-validation-httpcode="401" failed-validation-error-message="Unauthorized">
            <openid-config url="https://gainwell.okta.com/.well-known/openid-configuration" />
            <required-claims>
                <claim name="aud" match="all">
                    <value>https://fhir.gainwell.com</value>
                </claim>
                <claim name="scope" match="any">
                    <value>patient/*.read</value>
                    <value>patient/*.write</value>
                    <value>user/*.read</value>
                    <value>system/*.read</value>
                </claim>
            </required-claims>
        </validate-jwt>

        <!-- Extract patient context from JWT for compartment enforcement -->
        <set-variable name="patientId" value="@{
            var jwt = context.Request.Headers.GetValueOrDefault("Authorization", "").Replace("Bearer ", "");
            var token = jwt.Split('.')[1];
            var decoded = Encoding.UTF8.GetString(Convert.FromBase64String(token.PadRight(token.Length + (4 - token.Length % 4) % 4, '=')));
            var payload = JObject.Parse(decoded);
            return payload["patient"]?.ToString() ?? "";
        }" />

        <!-- Enforce patient compartment for patient/* scopes -->
        <choose>
            <when condition="@(context.Request.Headers.GetValueOrDefault("Authorization", "").Contains("patient/"))">
                <set-header name="X-Patient-Context" exists-action="override">
                    <value>@(context.Variables.GetValueOrDefault<string>("patientId"))</value>
                </set-header>

                <!-- Validate requested patient matches token patient -->
                <choose>
                    <when condition="@{
                        var requestPath = context.Request.Url.Path;
                        var requestPatient = "";
                        if (requestPath.Contains("/Patient/")) {
                            requestPatient = requestPath.Split(new[] { "/Patient/" }, StringSplitOptions.None)[1].Split('/')[0];
                        }
                        var tokenPatient = context.Variables.GetValueOrDefault<string>("patientId");
                        return !string.IsNullOrEmpty(requestPatient) && requestPatient != tokenPatient;
                    }">
                        <return-response>
                            <set-status code="403" reason="Forbidden" />
                            <set-body>{"error": "patient_compartment_violation", "message": "Cannot access data for different patient"}</set-body>
                        </return-response>
                    </when>
                </choose>
            </when>
        </choose>

        <!-- Rate limiting by client_id -->
        <rate-limit-by-key calls="100" renewal-period="60" counter-key="@(context.Request.Headers.GetValueOrDefault("Authorization", ""))" />

        <!-- Route to appropriate state FHIR server -->
        <set-backend-service base-url="@{
            var stateFHIRServers = new Dictionary<string, string> {
                {"CA", "https://fhir-ca.gainwell.com"},
                {"TX", "https://fhir-tx.gainwell.com"},
                {"NY", "https://fhir-ny.gainwell.com"}
            };
            var state = context.Request.Headers.GetValueOrDefault("X-State-Code", "CA");
            return stateFHIRServers.GetValueOrDefault(state, "https://fhir-default.gainwell.com");
        }" />
    </inbound>

    <backend>
        <forward-request timeout="30" />
    </backend>

    <outbound>
        <!-- Add SMART conformance headers -->
        <set-header name="X-SMART-Version" exists-action="override">
            <value>1.0.0</value>
        </set-header>

        <!-- Audit log FHIR access -->
        <log-to-eventhub logger-id="fhir-audit-logger">@{
            var jwt = context.Request.Headers.GetValueOrDefault("Authorization", "").Replace("Bearer ", "");
            var token = jwt.Split('.')[1];
            var decoded = Encoding.UTF8.GetString(Convert.FromBase64String(token.PadRight(token.Length + (4 - token.Length % 4) % 4, '=')));
            var payload = JObject.Parse(decoded);

            return new JObject(
                new JProperty("timestamp", DateTime.UtcNow),
                new JProperty("client_id", payload["client_id"]),
                new JProperty("patient", payload["patient"]),
                new JProperty("fhirUser", payload["fhirUser"]),
                new JProperty("resource", context.Request.Url.Path),
                new JProperty("method", context.Request.Method),
                new JProperty("status", context.Response.StatusCode),
                new JProperty("ip", context.Request.IpAddress)
            ).ToString();
        }</log-to-eventhub>
    </outbound>

    <on-error>
        <return-response>
            <set-status code="500" reason="Internal Server Error" />
            <set-body>{"error": "server_error", "message": "FHIR request processing failed"}</set-body>
        </return-response>
    </on-error>
</policies>
```

**HAPI FHIR SMART Interceptor**:

```java
// HAPI FHIR Server: SMART Authorization Interceptor
package com.gainwell.fhir.security;

import ca.uhn.fhir.rest.api.server.RequestDetails;
import ca.uhn.fhir.rest.server.interceptor.auth.AuthorizedList;
import ca.uhn.fhir.rest.server.interceptor.auth.IAuthRule;
import ca.uhn.fhir.rest.server.interceptor.auth.RuleBuilder;
import ca.uhn.fhir.rest.server.interceptor.auth.AuthorizationInterceptor;
import io.jsonwebtoken.*;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Component;

import java.util.List;

@Component
public class SMARTAuthorizationInterceptor extends AuthorizationInterceptor {

    @Override
    public List<IAuthRule> buildRuleList(RequestDetails theRequestDetails) {
        // Extract JWT from Authorization header
        String authHeader = theRequestDetails.getHeader("Authorization");
        if (authHeader == null || !authHeader.startsWith("Bearer ")) {
            return new RuleBuilder().denyAll().build();
        }

        String token = authHeader.substring(7);
        Claims claims;

        try {
            // Validate JWT signature and expiration (public key from JWKS endpoint)
            claims = Jwts.parserBuilder()
                .setSigningKeyResolver(new OktaJWKSKeyResolver())
                .build()
                .parseClaimsJws(token)
                .getBody();
        } catch (JwtException e) {
            // Invalid token
            return new RuleBuilder().denyAll().build();
        }

        // Extract SMART scopes from token
        String scopeString = claims.get("scope", String.class);
        String[] scopes = scopeString != null ? scopeString.split(" ") : new String[0];

        RuleBuilder ruleBuilder = new RuleBuilder();

        // Process patient/* scopes (patient compartment access)
        String patientId = claims.get("patient", String.class);
        if (patientId != null) {
            for (String scope : scopes) {
                if (scope.startsWith("patient/")) {
                    String[] parts = scope.split("/");
                    if (parts.length == 2) {
                        String resourceAndPermission = parts[1];  // e.g., "Observation.read"
                        String[] resourceParts = resourceAndPermission.split("\\.");
                        String resourceType = resourceParts[0];
                        String permission = resourceParts.length > 1 ? resourceParts[1] : "*";

                        if ("*".equals(resourceType)) {
                            // patient/*.read grants read access to all patient compartment resources
                            if ("read".equals(permission) || "*".equals(permission)) {
                                ruleBuilder.allow().read().allResources()
                                    .inCompartment("Patient", patientId).andThen();
                            }
                            if ("write".equals(permission) || "*".equals(permission)) {
                                ruleBuilder.allow().write().allResources()
                                    .inCompartment("Patient", patientId).andThen();
                            }
                        } else {
                            // patient/Observation.read grants read access to specific resource type
                            if ("read".equals(permission) || "*".equals(permission)) {
                                ruleBuilder.allow().read().resourcesOfType(resourceType)
                                    .inCompartment("Patient", patientId).andThen();
                            }
                            if ("write".equals(permission) || "*".equals(permission)) {
                                ruleBuilder.allow().write().resourcesOfType(resourceType)
                                    .inCompartment("Patient", patientId).andThen();
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        // Process user/* scopes (provider role-based access)
        String fhirUser = claims.get("fhirUser", String.class);  // e.g., "Practitioner/provider-456"
        if (fhirUser != null) {
            for (String scope : scopes) {
                if (scope.startsWith("user/")) {
                    String[] parts = scope.split("/");
                    if (parts.length == 2) {
                        String resourceAndPermission = parts[1];
                        String[] resourceParts = resourceAndPermission.split("\\.");
                        String resourceType = resourceParts[0];
                        String permission = resourceParts.length > 1 ? resourceParts[1] : "*";

                        if ("*".equals(resourceType)) {
                            // user/*.read grants read based on practitioner role
                            if ("read".equals(permission) || "*".equals(permission)) {
                                ruleBuilder.allow().read().allResources().andThen();
                            }
                        } else {
                            if ("read".equals(permission) || "*".equals(permission)) {
                                ruleBuilder.allow().read().resourcesOfType(resourceType).andThen();
                            }
                            if ("write".equals(permission) || "*".equals(permission)) {
                                ruleBuilder.allow().write().resourcesOfType(resourceType).andThen();
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        // Process system/* scopes (backend services bulk access)
        for (String scope : scopes) {
            if (scope.startsWith("system/")) {
                String[] parts = scope.split("/");
                if (parts.length == 2) {
                    String resourceAndPermission = parts[1];
                    String[] resourceParts = resourceAndPermission.split("\\.");
                    String resourceType = resourceParts[0];
                    String permission = resourceParts.length > 1 ? resourceParts[1] : "*";

                    if ("*".equals(resourceType)) {
                        if ("read".equals(permission) || "*".equals(permission)) {
                            ruleBuilder.allow().read().allResources().andThen();
                        }
                    } else {
                        if ("read".equals(permission) || "*".equals(permission)) {
                            ruleBuilder.allow().read().resourcesOfType(resourceType).andThen();
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        // Deny all other access
        return ruleBuilder.denyAll().build();
    }
}
```

**Best For**: Enterprise deployments requiring high scalability, multi-state isolation, comprehensive audit logging, and full SMART specification compliance.

