### Example 1: Member Mobile App with SMART Standalone Launch

**Context:** California Medicaid members use Gainwell Go™ mobile app to view health records, claims history, and prescription information.

**Requirements:**
- 850,000 registered members accessing FHIR APIs via iOS/Android mobile apps
- CMS Patient Access API compliance (45 CFR 170.315(g)(10))
- Granular consent: members authorize specific data types
- Offline access: app works without constant re-authentication
- Security: no hard-coded credentials, tokens stored in platform secure storage

**SMART Implementation:**

```typescript
// Gainwell Go Mobile App: SMART Standalone Launch
import { authorize, refresh } from 'react-native-app-auth';

const SMART_CONFIG = {
  issuer: 'https://oauth.gainwell.com',
  clientId: 'gainwell-go-mobile-ca',
  redirectUrl: 'com.gainwell.go://oauth/callback',
  scopes: ['patient/*.read', 'offline_access'],
  additionalParameters: {
    aud: 'https://fhir-ca.gainwell.com'
  }
};

async function authenticateMember() {
  const authResult = await authorize(SMART_CONFIG);
  await SecureStore.setItemAsync('access_token', authResult.accessToken);
  await SecureStore.setItemAsync('refresh_token', authResult.refreshToken);
  await SecureStore.setItemAsync('patient_id', authResult.tokenAdditionalParameters.patient);
  return authResult;
}
```

**Outcomes:**
- **CMS Compliance Achieved**: Passed ONC Inferno test suite; California Medicaid certified Q2 2024
- **Member Adoption**: 850K registered users (68% of eligible members); 4.7/5 app store rating
- **Security**: Zero credential theft incidents since SMART implementation
- **Consent Completion**: 87% completion rate vs. 52% with generic OAuth
